// The lessons, in order (#290), and after them the list of things to try in
// town (#303). Reorder, reword, add or remove one here; no
// code holds a lesson of its own. When several are waiting, the one nearest
// the top is shown first, and one is shown at a time.
//
// A lesson is something the player watches happen or does on the real
// control, with one line beside it: never a page to read (the owner,
// 2026-10-11). It never makes a control unavailable. While its pop-up is up
// the game stops, on the road and in town, until Got it is pressed or its
// thing is done (owner, 2026-10-12, #353); none comes up over a fountain.
//
//   id       its name: how it is known once put away. No two the same.
//   due      what has to happen first. It counts the first time it happens
//            and never again, so a return to town does not replay a lesson.
//              Fight     an encounter began
//              Ability   a horse's ability fired
//              Kill      an enemy went down
//              Resisted  a hit was resisted by its enemy's element
//              Win       a trail was won
//              Gear      the party came back to town with a piece
//              Card      the player opened a piece's card
//              Equipped  the player put a piece on a horse
//              Selected  the player selected another horse
//              Swapped   the player's Equip took a piece from the horse that
//                        wore it
//              SetOut    the party left town
//              Several   the party came back to town with more than one
//                        piece
//              Another   the player opened the card of a carried piece
//                        that is not the newest
//              Detailed  the player read a piece's card with its Details on
//              Dragged   the player put a piece on a horse by dragging it
//              Boss      a trail's boss fight began: its last encounter
//              Chose     the player gave a horse another ability
//              Mapped    the player opened the Map
//   fight    left out, or a number: the event counts only from that fight
//            on, counted from 1 since the game began. `due: Kill, fight: 2`
//            is the first kill of the second fight.
//   shown    where: Town, Road, or left out for either. A Town lesson that
//            is showing when the party sets out waits for the next town,
//            and is not offered by itself after it is left a second time.
//   target   the control its mark is on, named as places.ron names it:
//              Place("Journal")        a place in the bar, or Settings
//              Tab("Horses", "Gear")   a tab of a place
//              Control("Equip")        a control, wherever it is drawn
//              Horse(0)                a horse of the party, counted from 0
//              Selected                the horse that is selected, its tag in the scene
//              Drop                    the newest piece a trail brought back
//                                      that the party still has, where it is
//                                      now: in the cargo, or on a horse
//              Party                   the party as a whole: the line alone,
//                                      with no mark on any control
//              Boss                    the boss in the scene, while its fight
//                                      is on: the pop-up points at it
//              Resisted                the horse whose ability was resisted
//                                      the most on the last trail
//              Equipped                the horse a piece was last put on this
//                                      town visit, while that change stands
//            A lesson whose target is not there waits until it is.
//   words    its one line, said after the target's name and key, and by
//            itself in the Journal's list of hints (#300). Short: at
//            the smallest window the line has room for about a hundred
//            letters, the name included, and a piece's name is long. The
//            game fills in two things (#298): {change}, the stat of the
//            horse a piece last went on that moved the most, as it was and
//            as it is ("attack 12 to 15 and 2 more"), and {level}, the trail
//            level. No line claims what the report cannot show: stats and
//            levels, never "easier" or "better" (a test holds a list).
//   done     what finishes it:
//              Watched(Kill)  that happens while the lesson is showing.
//                             The game stops under a lesson (#353), so
//                             one on the road is answered by Got it
//              Did(Equipped)  that happens once the lesson is due, shown or
//                             not: the player needed no telling
//   instead  the line to say when the state has moved on: when a Drop is
//            no longer in the cargo but on a horse; or, for a line with
//            {change}, when no piece was put on a horse this visit.
//
// A lesson shown in town is answered by doing its thing, never by Got it
// alone (owner, 2026-10-19, #372: "ALL in-town hints MUST require the user
// to do something"): its done is a Did, and its pop-up has no Got it.
//
// The first is the opening's (#292). The next two are a starting set, from docs/philosophy/onboarding.md; the
// first trail's lessons are #295 and the element's #299. The rest are the
// first item's (#296): the piece, whose stats its card is about, Equip, and
// what came of it. Each is finished by doing the thing, and none has to be.
//
// `list` is the things to try in town (#303): a short list over the town
// scene, each entry one thing to do on the real controls. It is ticked when
// the player does the thing in town, by pointer or by key, and by nothing
// else, and pays its coins once. None has to be done; one left undone is
// there at the next town. Add, remove, reorder or reprice one here. A later
// feature adds its own entry as its tutorial.
//
//   id     its name. No two the same.
//   due    what has to happen before it is on the list: an event, as above.
//   words  the thing to do, in one line of 32 letters at most. Never a
//          control that is not built.
//   done   the player's doing this ticks it. As above, and three that are
//          only ever the player's:
//            Compared  another horse was selected with a piece's card open
//            Toured    every place in the bar has been opened, counted from
//                      when an entry asks for it
//            SentOut   Set out was pressed; Keep going's own departure is
//                      not this
//   coins  what it pays. Tuning.
//
// `skipped` is what Skip all hints is answered with, once and never again
// (#350): where the hints went and what turns them back on. It is on the
// hint's line with Got it beside it, holds nothing up, and goes when the
// player gets there or turns hints on. The Hints switch in Settings says so
// itself and does not raise it.
//
//   target  where the hints are found again, as a lesson's target is named.
//           A tab's mark is on its place too, while that place is not open.
//   words   its one line, said after the target's name and key: 85 letters
//           at most.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
(
lessons: [
    // The opening (#292): a new game starts with the party walking out of
    // the gate, and this is the one line beside it. No mark, so nothing
    // looks as if it wants a press but its Got it.
    (
        id: "the horses go by themselves",
        due: SetOut,
        shown: Road,
        target: Party,
        words: "You organise the gaggle. The horses walk, fight and collect loot by themselves.",
        done: Watched(Fight),
    ),
    (
        id: "the party fights by itself",
        due: Fight,
        shown: Road,
        target: Horse(0),
        words: "The horses fight by themselves. Nothing in a fight needs a press.",
        done: Watched(Kill),
    ),
    (
        id: "abilities fire by themselves",
        due: Ability,
        shown: Road,
        target: Horse(2),
        words: "Each horse has one ability, and uses it by itself when it is ready.",
        done: Watched(Ability),
    ),
    // The damage numbers (#249), once the first fight has shown some: read
    // by watching the next kill's.
    (
        id: "the numbers are hits",
        due: Kill,
        shown: Road,
        target: Horse(1),
        words: "Each number is a hit, sized by damage, coloured by element; a minus is a horse hit.",
        done: Watched(Kill),
    ),
    // Speed (#355), on the fastest of the starting party, whose hits come
    // the most often: seen in the hits around it once the game goes on. At
    // fight 2's first kill, so it never follows the numbers back to back
    // (#293 call 5).
    (
        id: "speed",
        due: Kill,
        fight: 2,
        shown: Road,
        target: Horse(0),
        words: "The faster a horse, the more often it hits. The party walks at their average speed.",
        done: Watched(Kill),
    ),
    // The boss (#360): on it as its fight begins, the first time only.
    (
        id: "the boss",
        due: Boss,
        shown: Road,
        target: Boss,
        words: "The trail's boss: its last fight, and the one with the best loot.",
        done: Watched(Win),
    ),
    (
        id: "press the piece",
        due: Gear,
        shown: Town,
        target: Drop,
        words: "The trail brought this back. Press it and its card opens.",
        done: Did(Card),
        // Said when it was put on a horse without its card being opened.
        instead: "It is on a horse now. Press it and its card opens.",
    ),
    (
        id: "the card is about the selected horse",
        due: Card,
        shown: Town,
        target: Selected,
        words: "The selected horse: the card's before and after are its. Press another horse.",
        done: Did(Selected),
    ),
    // Every kill throws gear (#352): the first trail brings back several
    // pieces, and the choice is among them. Taught by opening another.
    (
        id: "choose among them",
        due: Several,
        shown: Town,
        target: Place("Inventory"),
        words: "The trail brought back more than one piece. Open another's card: you choose.",
        done: Did(Another),
    ),
    // Nothing equips by itself (#351): leaving it is valid, and loses nothing.
    // On Another horse (#356): Equip beside it names the selected horse, and
    // this opens the list of the others, so the choice of who is seen.
    (
        id: "equip or leave it",
        due: Card,
        shown: Town,
        target: Control("Another horse"),
        words: "You choose who: Equip's, or another from this list. Left alone, it stays carried.",
        done: Did(Equipped),
    ),
    // Abilities carry their elements (#357): at the first resisted hit, in
    // town where it can be changed, on the horse whose ability it was.
    // Done by giving a horse another ability.
    (
        id: "a resisted ability",
        due: Resisted,
        shown: Town,
        target: Resisted,
        words: "Its ability's element was resisted. Select it, then Abilities [2] to change it.",
        done: Did(Chose),
    ),
    // The opening's exit line (#298): what the party does next by itself,
    // and that it can be left to it, answered by opening the Map (#372). On
    // the Map, where the itinerary will be: Keep going stands in for it and
    // nothing may depend on it (places.ron), so only these words name it,
    // and change when #201 ships.
    (
        id: "it can be left",
        due: Win,
        shown: Town,
        target: Place("Map"),
        words: "Keep going here sends the party out by itself till a trail is lost. Open it to see.",
        done: Did(Mapped),
    ),
    // The next trail, explained honestly (#298), last in town, on Set out
    // where the footer says the level, and answered by setting out (#372):
    // what the piece changed on the horse it went on, as it was and as it
    // is, and the level the win raised. The numbers, never that a fight
    // will go better. With nothing put on a horse this visit, the level
    // alone.
    (
        id: "set out to try it",
        due: Win,
        shown: Town,
        target: Control("Set out"),
        words: "{change} with it on. Trail level {level} now: set out to try it.",
        done: Did(SentOut),
        instead: "A win raises the trail level, now {level}: enemies and pieces gain stats. Set out.",
    ),
],
list: [
    (id: "select another horse", due: Gear, words: "Select another horse.", done: Selected, coins: 2),
    (id: "press the piece", due: Gear, words: "Press the new piece.", done: Card, coins: 2),
    (id: "compare on another horse", due: Gear, words: "Card open, select another horse.", done: Compared, coins: 3),
    (id: "equip it", due: Gear, words: "Put the piece on a horse.", done: Equipped, coins: 3),
    // The card's third layer (#228): its formulas, once a card has been seen.
    (id: "read the details", due: Card, words: "Open a piece, press Details [V].", done: Detailed, coins: 2),
    // Dragging (#228), the equal of Equip, once Equip has been done.
    (id: "drag a piece", due: Equipped, words: "Drag a piece onto a horse.", done: Dragged, coins: 2),
    (id: "open every place", due: Gear, words: "Open every place in the bar.", done: Toured, coins: 5),
    (id: "set out", due: Gear, words: "Set out.", done: SentOut, coins: 2),
],
skipped: (
    target: Tab("Journal", "Hints"),
    words: "Kept here, on the Journal. Hints in Settings brings them and the things to try back.",
),
)
